  "scope": "Darwin anonymous streams, real kqueue and relay. Guest connect outcome and TCP-only options are substituted. One warmup per arm, 12 balanced randomized pairs. Each arm verifies 512 immediate and 512 asynchronous connections per pair, 98 request and 148 response bytes per flow. Thread CPU covers adoption and the first drain, then the response and close drains for lifecycle. Setup counter counts filter-change syscalls. The fixture does not measure guest TCP timing.",
  "qualification": "ASan and UBSan, both owner types, both batch settings, both read-registration settings. Exercises retry, revocation, failed registration, both directions under backpressure, idle wakeup after the handshake, ordered delivery and FIN.",
